--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The driver is linked against the libraries below. Which of them a given
build actually contains depends on the backends it was configured with;
`strings <driver> | grep argus-build` names them for a released binary.

Several are covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License. The driver
links them dynamically, so a recipient may replace them with a modified
version, as section 4 of the LGPL requires. Their sources are available
from the projects named below and from the distribution that packaged
them.

  GLib, GObject, GIO                      LGPL-2.1-or-later
  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib     Object model, main loop, sockets

  json-glib                               LGPL-2.1-or-later
  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/json-glib

  Apache Thrift (C GLib runtime)          Apache-2.0
  https://thrift.apache.org               HiveServer2 / Impala protocol

  libcurl                                 curl licence (MIT/X derivative)
  https://curl.se                         Trino, Phoenix, Pinot, Druid,
                                          BigQuery, Thrift-over-HTTP

  unixODBC                                LGPL-2.1-or-later / GPL-2.0
  https://www.unixodbc.org                Driver manager headers (sql.h,
                                          sqlext.h, sqltypes.h)

  MariaDB Connector/C                     LGPL-2.1-or-later
  https://mariadb.com/kb/en/mariadb-connector-c/
                                          MySQL-wire backend (StarRocks,
                                          Doris, ClickHouse)

  libpq (PostgreSQL client library)       PostgreSQL Licence
  https://www.postgresql.org              PostgreSQL, Greenplum, Cloudberry

  MIT Kerberos (krb5, GSSAPI)             MIT
  https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/           Kerberos and SPNEGO authentication

  OpenSSL                                 Apache-2.0
  https://www.openssl.org                 Service-account signing (BigQuery),
                                          PKCE

  Apache Arrow, Arrow Flight SQL          Apache-2.0
  https://arrow.apache.org                Arrow Flight SQL backend

  Apache Kudu C++ client                  Apache-2.0
  https://kudu.apache.org                 Kudu backend

  cmocka (tests only, not distributed)    Apache-2.0
  https://cmocka.org

The Thrift IDL files under thrift/ are from the Apache Hive and Apache
Impala projects, Apache-2.0.
